oss the zebra crossing  hold on to me because i can see  something you can't  i can see something about you that you  yourself can't see  and so it's in having the privilege of  talking to students over and over again  and having  the opportunity to assure them and say  you're on a trajectory  there's a part of you that is not  defined  by your circumstances and actually the  circumstances of anything they're going  to make you stronger  and i don't want you to lose hope i  don't want you to give up that's a  lovely thing to say to kids  what you were going through at the time  seems horribly unfair i don't know if  unfair is the right word for it eddie  but it's awful it's always it was awful  for you  as a kid now your church has a lot to  say about suffering  do you think about that a lot did you  talk about that a lot in your church  yeah yeah we did i mean i i'd probably  say  it was that bedrock of knowing  from from the bible as a christian that  uh  one of the most important things in what  christians believes is that god is god  is sovereign he has  control things don't happen by accident  and  so even though from one angle you might  say well  you know there are terrible things  happening god why are you doing this  to me at the same time i know just from  the distance from me to my kids i  will frequently put my children through  things they do not want to do  i will hold them down as they fight and  kick as  a doctor or a nurse punctures their skin  with a needle  and immunizes them from all these  diseases and i'll say  you don't want this but this is what you  need  and to know that if that's the way i  regard my children if god is so much  wiser than i am  compared to me to my children i know  that what i'm going through if it's  my my mom being torn away from me or  these experiences of being younger and  and being treated in these harsh  and and cruel ways uh those things  shaped me and formed me and they've made  me who i am today  i said right at 